  "interpretation": "<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100.028%;\" border=\"1\"><colgroup><col style=\"width: 49.9303%;\"><col style=\"width: 49.9303%;\"></colgroup>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>RESULT IN U/mL&nbsp;</td>\n<td>REMARKS</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>&lt;9</td>\n<td>Negative</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>9-11</td>\n<td>Equivocal</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>&gt;11</td>\n<td>Positive</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">Note</span></strong><br><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">Equivocal results should be retested after 2-4 weeks.</span><br><strong><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">Comments</span></strong><br><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">Infectious mononucleosis is an acute lymphoproliferative disease common in children and young adults caused by Epstein Barr Virus (EBV) which is one of the Herpes viruses </span><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">4. VCA IgG antibodies occur early in the disease, reach highest titres within 2-4 weeks and persist for many years, maybe lifelong in some individuals</span></p>",
